Z||000002||stimpy||06-18-2000||04:50 PM||||Hey Monkey, what is your glitch regarding fathers day?  I know all of the sacrifices my father made to provide for his family did not come easy, and I see no reason not to have a special time to honor his role in society. I also saw the post you made in the other fathers day thread. I don't understand your bitterness, and personally it pains me that you would tarnish our gifts to our fathers. <BR>What's up with that? Maybe there are threads that you should refrain from posting on. I'm not mad, just disappointed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BENGAL4||06-18-2000||09:10 PM||||I don't know why MM is down on fathers day, but I respect his opinion. My dad would never read this, but I want to thank him for giving me my love of sports and making me work on my own cars.<P>He let me make a golf course out of our yard. He let me put goalposts in the backyard and I developed into a pretty good placekicker and punter. He put up a basketball hoop when I was 6. He let our yard be the playground of the neighborhood. He said he would have a nice yard after we grew up. The main thing I love about him is the fact he NEVER ONCE PUSHED SPORTS ON ME. He always let do what I wanted to do, within reason. It didn't matter to him whether I played sports or not. As long as I was happy, he didn't care. He noticed that I liked football, so he bought season tickets to the Bengals. I have been to almost every home game since 1970. Finally, he made me work on my first car and taught me patience. Thanks Dad.||||reg||10
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||06-18-2000||10:04 PM||||I will say THANKS gkozlov, I am a father and would like to say that the DXR Family always<BR>does it up for me on fathers day and I love every minute of it, and it's good to know that my children care enough to hang out with me and do some of the things they know I like, and buy me Fiero Stuff!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> My father in no longer with me, and as I think of him on this day all I have is good thoughts and remember all the good times we had, and hope that my kids will also have them of me.<P>HAPPY FATHERS DAY TO ALL THE DADS!!!<BR>FROM: DXR_DAD!!!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Monkeyman||06-19-2000||10:44 AM||||I apologize for my post.  I don't care for Fathers Day for a couple of reasons.  1st--I haven't had any contact with my father in about 25 years (I'm 32).  2nd--I don't get a chance to see my son very often as he doesn't live with me.  I shouldn't have posted what I did.  My problems shouldn't be everyone elses.  Please accept my apologies.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000006||gkozlov||06-19-2000||12:43 PM||||MonkeyMan<BR>My apalogies. I didnt know it was a touchy subject. I will in the future be more careful in my posts. Once again my apalogies to any one who might have been offended.<BR>gkozlov||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||06-19-2000||12:56 PM||||gkozlov--Absolutely no need for you to apologize.  It's me who should be sorry.  (I am/I posted.)  You were well within your rights to wish everyone a Happy Fathers Day.  I shouldn't have said anything.  I keep thinking I'm over all of that, but about once a year (on Fathers Day), I find myself feeling slightly depressed and alot more than slightly mad.  The rest of my feelings I'll save for the shrink. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
